ights  in Las Vegas which I just started  thought like I don't really feel like a  Vegas guy I'm certainly not a Vegas  performer but I just thought I'm  thinking I gotta get a picture of this  this is amazing this may never happen  again  since then like a regular in Vegas with  carrot top we can actually do together  where I saw him in half then I don't put  it back together again this is the  lead-up to the tour we did rehearsals in  his giant space in the valley  it's a giant rehearsal space in the Maui  huge mammoth space and we were trying to  figure out what this show was really  when we put it together so quickly I  remember being in this giant space and  there was hardly anyone there's a couple  of my writers you know Mike Sweeney and  a couple of other writers and and Jeff  Ross sitting maybe 50 feet away from me  and I'd do something that I thought was  kind of funny and then you'd hear  nothing and you'd feel like oh my god  this idea is terrible then later on you  find out well no they were laughing like  screaming you're alone there's a writer  Matt O'Brien I regularly I was about to  say used to beat him up by realizing now  I still do Pat just attack him regularly  but I'd see him and I just start  attacking him and he it was just an  obsession of Mike's I grew up in a big  family a lot of brothers and we would  fight each other all the time kind of  from play fighting so this was a really  fun shot at me backstage I was always  backstage fighting Matt O'Brien Here I  am again wearing it I must have  admittin or something mechana debris and  whalers shirt and a backstage again  fighting Matt O'Brien I look like I sort  of look like Conor McGregor in this shot  if Conor McGregor had leukemia I was  walking around somewhere I think  Vancouver and I bought myself a Greek  fisherman's cab I found an eyepatch and  I put that on and then I got myself a  little sea captain's flight so I might  before I wore that for a while and this  is a man who needs a be